{
  "comment": "Same plugin-panel pattern as the mopho/jv1080/d110 layouts. Rows follow the AWM2 signal path: voice common (element mode 1/2/4, volume, bend, output, element enable, controller routing) -> element level/pan/limits -> wave + pitch -> pitch EG -> filters 1 & 2 (series; filter 1 may be LPF/HPF, filter 2 LPF only) + their EGs and key scaling -> amp EG + level scaling -> LFO -> voice effect. All element groups share one select var {e} (select.shared = 'element', 'all' writes all four elements); in 1- or 2-element mode elements 3-4 (or 2-4) are not in the voice and edits to them go nowhere. Envelopes are Yamaha rate/level (rates 0-63, pitch/filter levels -64..+63, amp levels 0-63), so they are plain knobs in time order, not DADSR env cells. Amp EG in 'hold' mode turns r1 into a hold time. Effect params 1-3 mean different things per effect type (tg55.json effectTypes). Element enable toggles are live mutes, not stored in the voice. The voice name is edited in the name field (name1-10 are the ascii params).",
